{"kind":"propose","text":"Adopt docs/how-to/use-in-a-cloned-repo.md, and authorize its merge on independent review alone without a second adoption step.\n\nTHE CHOICE THIS ASKS HUGH TO MAKE, in one sentence: that this page is the one we ship for someone evaluating gitseq inside a repository they already have, and that his own two-gate process for it collapses to one.\n\nWHY THIS IS A PROPOSAL AND NOT THE ASSERT I FILED EARLIER. I asked hugh to ratify assert 225e5f9f to give the implementing commit a ratified decision. He could not find it in the UI, and the UI was right. The awaiting-ratification tab is built by ratificationRows in ui/src/lib/rows.ts, gated on awaitsRatification at line 323: satisfier is role:ratifier AND render is not note. The live vocabulary gives assert satisfier role:ratifier but render note, so it is excluded by design; propose has render proposal and is included. The comment above that function says why, and it is right: what is owed is a kind that does nothing until ratified, and an assert is a note that takes force on recording. Ratifying the assert was possible and close to meaningless — a ratification no queue would ever have shown him. This is the kind that carries a decision.\n\nIt also happens to be what hugh's own recorded process asked for. Assert 1e0d9a8d says each note is written, independently agent-reviewed, then ends with hugh's review as an adoption proposal resting on the note's artifact, ratified by hugh, before merge. This is that proposal, filed one step earlier in the order than he described, for a reason stated below.\n\nWHAT IS BEING ADOPTED. The page at docs/how-to/use-in-a-cloned-repo.md, plus one line in docs/README.md, on branch request/use-in-cloned-repo-howto. Original head 1aa0ce6d, rebased cleanly onto current main 6359f289 as a9b9427c840a9b949b750406af5b8475432d3424. Two files, 535 added lines, nothing deleted.\n\nWHAT I VERIFIED, so this is a decision on evidence rather than on my summary. Gates at the exact rebased head: gofmt silent, go build 0, go vet 0, git diff --check clean, go test ./... -count=1 with 32 packages ok and 0 failures, and go test ./internal/docset/... -count=1 ok in 70.138s.\n\nThat docset run is the load-bearing one. This page's commands are runnable sh blocks the documentation gate executes, including a block that writes eight bad resident.json records in turn, requires each to refuse before a signing key is read or anything is appended, and then asserts the log depth is unchanged so no refusal can pass by appending quietly. The page was written against de274aac and main has moved 44 commits since, so the question was whether its claims survived. They did, executed rather than read.\n\nTHE TWO CONSEQUENCES THIS ADOPTS, named because a proposal should say what it costs.\n\nFirst, the second gate goes. Hugh's process has independent agent review and then his own adoption judgement. Ratifying this proposal is that judgement, made now on the evidence above rather than after the review, so the page merges when a reviewer approves it and no further act from hugh is needed. If he would rather keep both gates, he should decline this and say so; the lane still works, it is just slower by one round trip.\n\nSecond, this becomes the commit's basis. Once ratified, I will amend the implementing commit's Rests-On to name the ratification, re-run the gates at the new sha, publish the artifact at docs/how-to/use-in-a-cloned-repo.md, and request an urgent independent review. The commit currently rests on assert 1e0d9a8d, which is effective but never ratified and now stale and flagged describes_superseded_world — the identical defect codex refused the README head for this morning.\n\nWHY THE ORDER IS INVERTED FROM HIS DESCRIPTION. He wrote that the proposal rests on the note's artifact. It cannot, quite: the artifact belongs at the final head, and the final head's trailer needs this ratification to exist first. So this proposal rests on the behaviour it depends on — kernel 60319b74 for refs and appends, service 175210ba for the resident refusal behaviour the page documents, cmd/gitseq-mcp 8e2b7c8c for the adapter difference the page names — and cites the head explicitly instead. The artifact follows the ratification rather than preceding it. If hugh wants the literal order, the cost is one more supersession cycle on the artifact, which this lane has already paid four times on the README and I would rather not repeat here.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT DECIDE. It does not approve the prose against a reviewer's eye; the independent review still has to happen and can still request changes. It does not name a reviewer. And it does not touch the second GitHub note, docs/how-to/connect-github.md, which is a separate lane.","body":{"branch":"request/use-in-cloned-repo-howto","head":"a9b9427c840a9b949b750406af5b8475432d3424","path":"docs/how-to/use-in-a-cloned-repo.md"}}